## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests the ability to extend classic path DP problems with an additional resource constraint, evaluating proficiency in managing 3D DP states, path reconstruction via backtracking, and space optimization.

## Key Concepts
- 3D DP state (i, j, t) tracking exact t boosts used at position (i,j)
- Two transition options: boost or skip the current cell
- Path reconstruction by backtracking through the DP table
- Space optimization: reduce to two rows or maintain a compact parent pointer table

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithBoosts(grid, k, B) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: m }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(NEG))
  );
  dp[0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  if (k > 0) dp[0][0][1] = grid[0][0] + B;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        if (i > 0 && dp[i-1][j][t] !== NEG) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t] + grid[i][j]);
        }
        if (j > 0 && dp[i][j-1][t] !== NEG) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t] + grid[i][j]);
        }
        if (t > 0) {
          if (i > 0 && dp[i-1][j][t-1] !== NEG) {
            dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t-1] + grid[i][j] + B);
          }
          if (j > 0 && dp[i][j-1][t-1] !== NEG) {
            dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t-1] + grid[i][j] + B);
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const boosts = [];
  let i = n - 1, j = m - 1, t = k;
  while (i > 0 || j > 0) {
    const fromTop = i > 0 && dp[i][j][t] === dp[i-1][j][t] + grid[i][j];
    const fromLeft = j > 0 && dp[i][j][t] === dp[i][j-1][t] + grid[i][j];
    const boostedFromTop = i > 0 && t > 0 && dp[i][j][t] === dp[i-1][j][t-1] + grid[i][j] + B;
    const boostedFromLeft = j > 0 && t > 0 && dp[i][j][t] === dp[i][j-1][t-1] + grid[i][j] + B;

    if (boostedFromTop || boostedFromLeft) boosts.push([i, j]);
    if (boostedFromTop || (i > 0 && fromTop && !boostedFromTop)) { i--; }
    else if (j > 0) { j--; if (!boostedFromLeft && !fromLeft) t--; }
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n-1][m-1][k], boosts: boosts.reverse() };
}
```

## Complexity
- **Time:** O(n × m × k)
- **Space:** O(n × m × k) or O(m × k) with row optimization

## How It Works

Concise technical explanation of the mechanism.

## Key Points

- **DP State**: local[k], global[k] track ending vs non-ending subarrays
- **Transition**: local[k] = max(local[k]+a[i], global[k-1]+a[i]); global[k] = max(global[k], local[k])
- **Edge Handling**: cap K to n; initialize -inf; handles negative values

## Example

```javascript
function maxRevenue(A, K) {
  const n = A.length;
  if (n === 0 || K <= 0) return 0;
  K = Math.min(K, n);
  const global = new Array(K+1).fill(-Infinity);
  const local = new Array(K+1).fill(-Infinity);
  global[0] = 0;
  for (let x of A) {
    for (let k = K; k >= 1; k--) {
      local[k] = Math.max((local[k] !== -Infinity ? local[k] + x : -Infinity), global[k-1] + x);
      global[k] = Math.max(global[k], local[k]);
    }
  }
  return global[K];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests deriving a clean DP where subarray cost depends on endpoints, not internal aggregates, and requires careful index handling and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- DP state dp[i][t] for first i elements into t blocks
- Transition over split point p with endpoint cost |A[p+1]-A[i]| 
- Backpointer reconstruction for endpoints
- Time O(n^2 k), space O(nk) (can optimize with rolling arrays)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minEndPointPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) dp[i][1] = Math.abs(A[0] - A[i]);
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t - 1; i < n; i++) {
      for (let p = t - 2; p <= i - 1; p++) {
        const val = dp[p][t - 1] + Math.abs(A[p + 1] - A[i]);
        if (val < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let endpoints = [];
  let i = n - 1, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const p = par[i][t];
    endpoints.unshift([p + 1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  return { cost: dp[n - 1][k], endpoints };
}
```

